Agent Orchestrator v2: Cluster Architecture & Data Flow
Overview
Agent Orchestrator v2 uses a two-cluster architecture to separate concerns between fast in-memory operations and persistent data storage:

Valkey Cluster (Redis-compatible) - Fast in-memory pub/sub and signaling
Central Cache Service + Glide - Persistent storage with ServiceNow backend
Architecture Components
1. Valkey Cluster (In-Memory, Fast)
Location: valkey_pubsub.py

Purpose: Cross-worker interrupt signaling and real-time coordination

Configuration:

properties
VALKEY_HOST=host.docker.internal
VALKEY_PORT=6381
VALKEY_PASSWORD=
Key Features:

Pub/Sub Channel: ao:interrupt - broadcasts interrupt signals across all worker processes
Worker Coordination: Each uvicorn worker subscribes to the channel
TLS Support: Automatic mTLS in non-dev environments using CERT_PATH and KEY_PATH
Connection Pooling: Singleton async Redis client shared across the worker
Data Flow:

Interrupt Request → Worker A publishes to ao:interrupt channel
                 ↓
            Valkey Cluster
                 ↓
    All workers receive message (pub/sub broadcast)
                 ↓
    Only the worker owning the conversation acts on it
